--- body ---
## Context
Author request, 2026-10-27 raid: define a route to aider with the padme local LLM backend. The live
smoke of the headless seat doors (ticket 1256) found aider 0.86.2 installed but no door in
`skills/route/routes.json` (doors: claude-code, pi, codex, vibe). Pi already reaches padme's local
models through OpenAI-compatible providers declared in `~/.pi/agent/models.json` (`padme`,
`padme-strata`, `padme-35b`, `padme-mellum`, each with a `baseUrl`). aider speaks the same API via
`--model openai/<id> --openai-api-base <baseUrl>`, and has read-only modes (`--chat-mode ask`,
`--dry-run`, `--no-git`, `--read`).

## Exit criteria
- [ ] routes.json declares an `aider` door: a headless template (`--message`/`--message-file`, pinned
      `--model`, the base URL taken from one source — Pi's provider declaration or a routes.json field,
      never a second hand-copied IP), `seat_rails` that keep it from editing or committing, and a
      `families` entry marking padme models local (no cross-provider spend, no consent needed).
- [ ] scripts/gaze_seat.py launches an aider seat like the other doors (cap, worker line, `no report`
      on failure, a model id the server does not serve refused rather than silently substituted — the
      Pi defect of ticket 1262 must not recur here); stubbed tests, red first.
- [ ] One live smoke on padme's local backend: a seat reviews a fixture diff and a write/commit
      instruction leaves the tree unchanged; recorded in the PR body.
- [ ] The harness gate passes.

## Relevant files
skills/route/routes.json, scripts/gaze_seat.py, tests/test_gaze_seat.py, skills/route/routes-recommendations-*.md

Related: [[1256]], [[1262]].
